    <item>
      <title>Nuclear factor I connects H3K27M to a targetable purine dependency in diffuse intrinsic pontine glioma</title>
      <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-79694-0</link>
      <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Nature Communications, Published online: 26 November 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-79694-0"&gt;doi:10.1038/s41467-026-79694-0&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Diffuse intrinsic pontine glioma is an aggressive childhood cancer commonly driven by H3K27M with few treatment options. This study links H3K27M-driven chromatin remodelling to NFI-dependent purine metabolism, causing ATIC/PNP-mediated metabolic rewiring and ATIC-targetable tumour dependence.</content:encoded>
