    <item>
      <title>Plant protoplasts display phytopodia</title>
      <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-79550-1</link>
      <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Nature Communications, Published online: 26 November 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-79550-1"&gt;doi:10.1038/s41467-026-79550-1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Plant cells are encased in cell walls that when digested leave spherical protoplasts. Here the authors report long, thin membrane protrusions from protoplasts termed phytopodia and discuss their potential role in the probing behaviour of the cell cortex.</content:encoded>
